PHOTOGRAPHS — NOT covered by the CC BY grant
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Photographs in this repository are of mixed provenance. They are used with
credit for non-commercial educational purposes and are EXCLUDED from the CC BY
grant above, which covers text only.

We do not own most of these photographs and cannot sublicense them. Copying
this repository does not give you permission to reuse them. If you intend to
use a photograph for any purpose, trace it to its source and seek permission
from the rights holder.

Known sources:

  - web/images/extracted/ — submarine and commanding-officer photographs, most
    sourced via NavSource Naval History (navsource.org). NavSource aggregates
    material from many contributors, including US Navy and National Archives
    photographs and privately held collections. Each lost-boat record carries a
    per-image credit field, rendered beneath the image on the page. Where a
    contributor is known the credit names them; where it is not, the credit
    reads "Photo via NavSource Naval History", which records the route the
    image reached us by and not a claim about who holds the rights.

    web/images/extracted/ is the only image directory in this repository.
    Untraced images that were never published on the site were removed from
    the tree rather than shipped with unresolved provenance.

If you hold rights in any photograph here and want it credited differently or
removed, contact us and we will act on it. See SECURITY.md for contact details.

